cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MINFF: A forcefield for molecular simulations of minerals"
message: "If you use MINFF in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Holmboe
    given-names: Michael
    email: michael.holmboe@umu.se
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, Umeå University, Sweden"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mholmboe/minff"
url: "https://github.com/mholmboe/minff"
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  MINFF is a molecular dynamics forcefield for oxides and hydroxides containing
  Si, Al, Fe, Mg, Ca, Ti, Li and F, including hydrated clay minerals and
  zeolites. In addition to Lennard-Jones and Coulombic terms it uses angle
  terms to maintain coordination environments and unit cell metrics. MINFF is
  distributed as a general parameter set (GMINFF) and as mineral-specific
  tailored sets (TMINFF) covering over 30 minerals, each available for angle
  force constants of 0, 250, 500 and 1500 kJ/mol/rad^2.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - forcefield
  - clay minerals
  - zeolites
  - oxides
  - hydroxides
  - GROMACS
  - LAMMPS
